\section{Architecture and honest controls}
Fusion v2 is persistence anchored and decodes 5/15/30/60-minute horizons from
short, medium, and slow Cn²/weather histories. It uses causal temporal blocks,
horizon Fourier features, a scale router, four diagnostic experts, physical
refractivity/stability tokens, ordered quantiles, and a Student-\(t\) head.
The selected concatenative weather interaction cannot be suppressed by a
single final scalar gate. Related multi-horizon and exogenous-attention
architectures include TFT and TimeXer \cite{lim2020tft,wang2024timexer}; this
implementation is a custom adaptation, not a universal novelty claim.

Persistence and climatology are operational anchors. MLP, TCN, and Horizon v1
are neural controls on identical endpoints. LightGBM is retained only as a
diagnostic of learnable weather signal, never as the intended flagship.

